            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0701" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A European War/9–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-18T15:00:00-04:00">September 18,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1866. Last paragraph your 3700, September 16, 5 p.m. not clear. Do you mean (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) that Sweden will immediately release one
                    American airman for each German arriving on a Finnish vessel even though the
                    German will be interned for the duration or (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)
                    that one American airman will be released for each German arriving in this
                    manner who will be offered the choice of remaining in Sweden or returning to
                    Germany?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
